  "content": "# Implementing a Bounded LRU Cache in Python\n\n## Overview\n\nA **Least Recently Used (LRU) cache** is a memory management policy that discards the least recently used items when the cache reaches its capacity. This is widely used in databases, HTTP caches, and operating systems. Python\u2019s `collections.OrderedDict` provides an ideal foundation because it maintains insertion order (and more importantly, **access order** when using `move_to_end`) and supports O(1) operations for `popitem`, `move_to_end`, and dictionary access.\n\nBelow is a complete, production-quality implementation with thorough documentation, followed by tests, a worked example, and a complexity analysis.\n\n---\n\n## Complete Implementation\n\n```python\n\"\"\"\nA bounded LRU cache implemented using collections.OrderedDict.\n\nKey properties:\n- Fixed capacity at construction.\n- get(key) returns the value if present, marks the key as most recently used.\n- put(key, value) inserts or updates a key. If capacity is exceeded, the least\n  recently used key is evicted.\n- All operations (get, put, contains) are O(1) amortized.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\nfrom typing import Hashable, Any\n\n\nclass LRUCache:\n    \"\"\"\n    A Least Recently Used cache with a fixed maximum capacity.\n\n    Usage:\n        cache = LRUCache(capacity=3)\n        cache.put(\"a\", 1)\n        cache.put(\"b\", 2)\n        cache.put(\"c\", 3)\n        cache.get(\"a\")   # returns 1, \"a\" becomes most recently used\n        cache.put(\"d\", 4) # evicts \"b\" (least recently used)\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, capacity: int):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initialize the LRU cache.\n\n        Args:\n            capacity: Maximum number of items the cache can hold. Must be >= 1.\n\n        Raises:\n            ValueError: If capacity is less than 1.\n        \"\"\"\n        if capacity < 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"Capacity must be at least 1\")\n        self._capacity = capacity\n        self._store = OrderedDict()  # key -> value, ordered by LRU -> MRU\n\n    def get(self, key: Hashable) -> Any:\n        \"\"\"\n        Retrieve the value associated with the key.\n\n       ",
